Actually, it's a little worse than that!  Be careful with armor
enchantment.

Elven armor and wizard hats are a little more resiliant, so they are
relatively safer.  For all other armor, the safety point is +3!

So, what that means is, if you're wearing a +3 chain mail, and you read
a blessed scroll of enchant armor, there is a 2/3 chance (!) that it
will be evaporated.  What the hardcore spoiled nethacker does in this 
situation, is to DISENCHANT the armor to +2, and then read the blessed 
scroll for a max of +5.  If you are brave, foolish, and you have lots
of +5 armor to waste and extra scrolls, you can try for more.  If you're 
trying for +7 from +5, you have only a 1/5 chance of getting it, and a
4/5 chance of losing your armor.

>So how do the folks here get +7 armor? Could someone enlighten me?

Elven armor is easier to get to +7.  If you're reading YAAP's where
people have +7 or greater regular armor, it's probably because the
player got bored between the castle and waking up Rodney, and had 
too much loot for their own good.  I wouldn't try it in the early game,
because a piece of armor that's +3 is a lot more valuable than a piece
of armor that's evaporated.  I'd be more inclined to use the extra
scroll for fireproofing than enchantment.  OTOH, I do try to make
everything +5, in the rare games where I get the opportunity.


